From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:15:52 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] qwen3_5: resolve the mHC image only when the model has
 streams; accept f32 dt_bias

- cuda_mhc.install returns early for a model without mHC, so the family's own
  handles must still resolve: they do, the mHC four are gone from Fns.
- the bf16 attention tiles' dynamic shared memory opt-in is restored (it was
  lost while consolidating the resolve block, and every attention launch failed
  with CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE without it).
- loop_settings/mhc accept start 0 (a loop may begin at layer 0).
- dt_bias and the norms read an HF checkpoint's own dtype: f32 dt_bias widened
  to bf16, and the affine path keeps raw w (it does not add the 1).
